<section class="panel">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="eyebrow">Seven repositories, MIT and GPL</div>
		<h1>Contribute</h1>
		<p class="lede">Patches, recipes, build scripts and the reasoning behind every
		decision. Reporting a phone that boots, or does not, already helps.</p>
		<div class="grid">
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/utsugi-pmaports">
				<div class="n">utsugi-pmaports</div>
				<p>Packages, the 78 kernel patches, metapackages, build and publish
				scripts.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/poconav">
				<div class="n">poconav</div><p>Car navigation.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/screenglaze">
				<div class="n">screenglaze</div><p>Screenshots.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/keepalive">
				<div class="n">keepalive</div><p>Apps that minimise instead of closing.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/app-usage">
				<div class="n">app-usage</div><p>Battery per application.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/smart-unlock">
				<div class="n">smart-unlock</div><p>Skip the PIN when it is safe.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/lost-phone">
				<div class="n">lost-phone</div><p>Find the phone without Google.</p></a>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>01</span><h2>Build it</h2></div>
		<div class="sh">
			<div class="bar"><i></i><span>ON YOUR PC</span></div>
			<pre>git clone https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/utsugi-pmaports
cd utsugi-pmaports
scripts/setup-workdir   <i># own work dir, pinned pmaports, a signing key</i>
scripts/build --all     <i># the kernel takes about 20 minutes</i>
scripts/lint            <i># forks, version bumps, unreachable packages</i>
scripts/check-upstream  <i># says when a fork has fallen behind</i>
scripts/publish --push</pre>
		</div>
		<h3>Three rules that will bite otherwise</h3>
		<div class="scroll">
		<table>
			<tr><th>Always bump</th><td>pmbootstrap skips a build whose version already
			exists in any index it knows and reports success. Use
			<code>scripts/bump</code>.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Never move a tag</th><td>The old tarball stays in the distfile cache
			under the same name and the build silently uses it.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>The chroot builds as uid 12345</th><td>Anything it writes to must
			belong to <code>12345</code>: the signing key, the ccache. Both have cost a
			day.</td></tr>
		</table>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="panel">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>02</span><h2>How the packages are put together</h2></div>
		<p>A patched package is forked under its own name and claims upstream's with a
		versioned <code>provides</code>:</p>
		<div class="sh">
			<div class="bar"><i></i><span>APKBUILD</span></div>
			<pre>_orig=hexagonrpcd
pkgname=$_orig-utsugi
provides="$_orig=$pkgver-r$pkgrel"
replaces="$_orig"</pre>
		</div>
		<p>apk then refuses to have both installed, anything depending on
		<code>hexagonrpcd</code> is satisfied by ours, and an upstream release cannot
		quietly take its place.</p>
		<p>Each kernel patch carries its own write-up above the diff: what broke, what
		was measured, what was ruled out. If you send one, write it the same way.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>03</span><h2>Where help would land</h2></div>
		<div class="scroll">
		<table>
			<tr><th>Fingerprint</th><td>Four routes are documented dead ends. A fifth
			would be new ground.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Echo on calls</th><td>Tunable at runtime. Needs patience and a
			second phone.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>ADSP recovery deadlock</th><td>Takes the filesystem with it. The
			measurements are written up; the cause is not found.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Vayu modem</th><td>Pinned to one firmware assertion. Nobody has got
			past it.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Upstreaming</th><td>The GPS engine lock affects every Qualcomm device
			on postmarketOS. The dialpad fix belongs in KDE.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Stereo audio</th><td>Kernel work on
			<code>TERT_MI2S_RX</code>.</td></tr>
		</table>
		</div>
